<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21051] Set proper permissions on SSK keys</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21051</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When an SSK key is loaded into the keyring, either with lgss_sk -l or through the skpath mount option, sk_load_key() explicitly sets permissions on the new key. The client mount does the same when it renames the key per client in gss_rename_sk_key(). The mask used today is broader than what the SSK code needs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SSK keys are owned by root, and every consumer of them runs as root:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;the lgss_keyring upcall for SSK contexts, which are root-only&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lsvcgssd&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lgss_sk&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;the client mount&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;User permissions are therefore enough. The permissions set on these keys should be reduced to just those.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
